    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.91) and **Will Smith** (67.40) anchor the lineup as our most reliable options. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the two-hole against a vulnerable Leiter, while **Will Smith** draws a prime matchup against Kochanowicz, whose 5.12 xERA creates a massive ceiling for production. **Geraldo Perdomo** also warrants attention; despite the lower batting order spot, his efficiency (62.79) is bolstered significantly by a favorable matchup against Littell. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Taylor Ward**, whose score (43.45) is suppressing due to a negative platoon split despite his lead-off role, landing him just above our bench threshold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Bryson Stott** (48.56), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Bryson Stott** offers a slight bonus for his ability to swipe bags against a slow-delivering pitcher, his efficiency was capped by a negative platoon disadvantage against Eisert. We opted for higher individual category upside elsewhere, though the thin margin suggests he remains the first call should a late scratch occur. **Jung Hoo Lee** (49.14) remains in the lineup despite a mediocre raw score, as his profile\u2014specifically the combination of his park factors and the stolen base potential against Brown\u2014keeps him as a critical component in maintaining our league-leading speed production. \n\nA final note of caution: with several pitchers posting xERAs north of 4.00, we are banking on aggressive offensive output to mitigate risk. We have officially sidelined **Cal Raleigh** due to his IL designation, and should weather reports shift or lineups undergo late-afternoon adjustments, we may look to rotate **Matt Chapman** into the mix if the park factors improve. For now, the roster construction prioritizes high-efficiency matchups to maximize our 5x5 totals while preserving our limited daily game caps.",
